Undoubtedly there are many more bugs/enhancement needed, but these are the ones I know about:

Views can draw outside of the parent view's bounds (see Showcase, tab 3)
	You can click the edges of the Walter logo to move it around and see it
	"escape" the tab view.  When running Showcase on Haiku, it clips to the tab view
	as you would expect.

Closing any window causes Wayland apps to crash (now has hacky workaround in window.c)
	See surface_leave() in window.c

Cairo asserts on exit due to non-empty object hash (i.e. something didn't get disposed)

TextEdit control works but has issues
	Selection changes sometimes don't show up until the next repaint
	As you scroll down, parts of the view stop drawing (see AboutSystem)
	Large amounts of text cause redraw (and thus window resize) to be very slow

Window repaint is inefficient
	After any Invalidate(), the entire window backing buffer is copied

Apps using Layout are much more likely to crash

Some Be apps set their initial window size to 0,0,0,0 and it gets resized correctly
	We now have a mechanism to fix this in the backend message handler
	for AS_WINDOW_CREATE.
	This should be tested on Terminal and Pairs since they used to do
	this trick.

Alerts are sometimes shown too small to fit their contents

Asynchonous alerts hang the program
	Synchronous alerts called with Go(NULL) work, but the async ones called with Go() cause a hang.
	This is caused by the backend handlers calling FindView.  They should not call BWindow funcs.

Spawning an alert sometimes causes a crash

Modal alerts are not fully modal on Wayland
	The alert stays front-most, but input/clicks are allow in the parent window

BChannelSlider draws incorrectly
	It appears to have something to do with the hardcoded thumb images that are loaded as
	B_CMAP8 color space bitmaps.  Very rarely used, so not a big deal.

BColumnListView somehow accesses view states already popped and deleted by PopState()
	Somehow triggered by its CONSTRAIN_CLIPPING_REGION define, which I have now turned off.
	Eventually, this leads to a segfault.  This may be fixed as of 11/25/2025, but can't verify.

B_CMAP8 (and a few others) are not valid color spaces for drawing, due to lack of support in Cairo
	Should we auto-upgrade these color spaces to B_RGB32 at BBitmap creation to avoid issues, or
	would this just cause new ones?
	You can still set or import a BBitmap's bits with data from B_CMAP8 or other
	unsupported-for-drawing color spaces -- it will get correctly converted to the BBitmap's
	supported color space.

Menus don't track correctly, and pop-ups show but then hang the app (Mac only)

Windows GUI works but is unstable and flaky at this stage
	Fonts look distorted when you run in Wine.  In Windows they look normal.
	Apps crash or hang when you attempt to close them
	Pop-up menus hang the app

If you use an app for long enough it will eventually crash with a corrupt BMessage header
	Crash typically happens in UsePreferredTarget.  I've seen this on all platforms.
	Since this is almost completely unmodified Haiku code, I'm surprised they haven't seen this.

BRecentFilesList/BRecentFolderList are only partially implemented

Drag-n-Drop support is not yet implemented on any backend

get_mouse() is just an empty stub

WindowStack is just an empty stub


The following were known issues from Cosmoe Classic before forking to this project:

entry_ref's only work if Name holds an absolute path
	Converting from a BEntry or GetNextRef fills this out correctly, but considering how
	extensively entry_ref is used, it's certain this is causing issues somewhere.  I don't
	know of a specific problem though.

send_data() and receive_data() use a static, hard-coded 512 byte area to pass information
	The current implementation was a quick hack to get menus working, since they use this
	functionality extensively. I've never gone back and coded it to allocate memory dynamically.
	See src/system/kernel/thread.cpp
	To do this dynamically turns out to probably be harder than it's worth, as this is not used
	very often, and when it is, very small amounts of data are passed.

BVolume and BVolumeRoster need improvement
	BVolumeRoster gets filled out, but it's surprisingly tricky on Linux to get a list of only the 
	volumes a user would typically expect to see on a desktop.  So you'll end up with say /swapfile,
	but not	your mounted USB drive, for example.

Unit tests aren't even close to 100% passing
	We are now synced with Haiku unit tests.  Unfortunately, they use a custom unit test library that
	is a pain to work with, since determining exactly where a test failed is very time-consuming.
	I know this will be hugely valuable in making Cosmoe more stable and compliant though.

Cosmoe stubs out Haiku's BCatalog system for translating strings
	I think this would work fine if the Haiku catalogs were merged and installed, and the BCatalog
	(and friends) source was synced up with Haiku, but I just haven't seen this as a priority yet.

Sudoku just hangs now
off-by-one pixel debris in views
BTextView doesn't show edited text until resize

Pulse - Good
Showcase - Good
Mandelbrot - Good
Gradients - Good
Clock - Good
FontDemo - Good
DeskCalc - Good
minimal - Good
AboutSystem - Good
gui-torture - Good
